course: dictionary
lesson: 6245
title: The modem: your link to the internet
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A modem is the box that links your home to the internet. It connects through a phone line, cable or fibre, so the internet can reach your computer.
explain: In most homes, data goes from the computer to the router, then to the modem, and out along the line. Often the modem and router are one box, and that box also makes the Wi-Fi.
explain: Long ago, «In the 1990s many homes used dial-up modems, which screeched as they connected through the phone line and were very slow.» Using the internet meant nobody could use the house phone at the same time.
fact: A modem connects a computer or a home network to the internet.
fact: A modem can connect through a phone line, a cable or fibre.
fact: «Modem» is a noun: a modem, two modems.
fact: In the 1990s, dial-up modems could take about 30 seconds to connect, with beeps and screeches.
fact: When the internet is down, «turn the modem off and on again» is a common fix.
exercise: What does a modem do? | Stores your photos for ever | Prints pages onto paper | *Connects your computer or home network to the internet | Plays music through the speakers
exercise: «Turn the modem off and on again» is a common fix for what problem? | When the screen is too bright | When the printer runs out of paper | *When the internet is down | When you want a new game
exercise: «...which screeched as they connected through the phone line...» Find and copy the word that means made a loud, harsh sound. | connected | *screeched | phone | slow
test: At home, the modem is often also what? | A printer that prints in colour | A computer screen | *The same box as the router that makes the Wi-Fi | A game console
test: Why did dial-up take about 30 seconds to connect? | It was charging its battery | It was waiting for the sun to rise | It was printing a film | *It beeped and screeched while it connected
exam: In a home network, which device sends your data out along the line to the internet provider? | Keyboard | *Modem | Mouse | Speaker
